2) Battery life math: 

Powerbanks are rated in mAh at 3.7V. A 20,00 mAH bank holds 74 Wh
 Assume about 80% is usable after conversion so 59 Wh 
Runtime is usable Wh divided by total watts. so 5 hours in this case

Convert mAh to Wh:
power bank capacity: 20,000 mAh

          20,000 / 1,000 = 20Ah
          20Ah x 3.7 v = 74 Wh
Account for power loss:
Assume 80% is usable after conversion

          74 x 0.80 = 59.2 Wh

Calculate battery life 
          Battery Life = (usable Wh / Total Watts)
          59.2 / 13.4 = 4.42 

roughly around 4.4 hours of battery life 
